  "body": "Since last commit apparently, compilation fails in linux (Debian 13 stable, Manjaro), with the following message:\n```\nIn file included from /home/sguyader/Sources/ART/rtengine/rawimage_gainmap.cc:21:\n/home/sguyader/Sources/ART/rtengine/gainmap.h:48:10: error: \"string\" in namespace \"std\" does not name a type\n48 |     std::string to_str() const;\n   |          ^~~~~~\n/home/sguyader/Sources/ART/rtengine/gainmap.h:25:1: note: \"std::string\" is defined in the header \"<string>\"; this can likely be fixed by adding \"#include <string>\"\n24 | #include <vector>\n+++ |+#include <string>\n25 |\n[ 40%] Building CXX object rtengine/CMakeFiles/rtengine.dir/bayer_bilinear_demosaic.cc.o\nmake[2]: *** [rtengine/CMakeFiles/rtengine.dir/build.make:1759: rtengine/CMakeFiles/rtengine.dir/rawimage_gainmap.cc.o] Error 1\nmake[2]: *** Waiting for unfinished jobs....\nmake[1]: *** [CMakeFiles/Makefile2:190: rtengine/CMakeFiles/rtengine.dir/all] Error 2\nmake: *** [Makefile:136: all] Error 2\n\n```\n\nAdding `#include <string>` in `rtengine/gainmap.h` seems to work, but I don't know if it's the correct way to fix the issue.",
